Frequently Asked Questions
**Q: When should I enable DEV_ERROR_DETECT?**
A: Enable during development and testing to catch programming errors. Disable in production to reduce code size and improve performance, unless safety requirements dictate otherwise.
**Q: What happens if the module is not initialized before use?**
A: The behavior is undefined. The module must be initialized via EXP_LayeredSoftwareArchitecture_Init() before any other API calls. Most functions check initialization status and report errors if not 
```c /* Application Code with Error Handling */ void ProcessData(uint8 channelId) { Std_ReturnType status; uint8 data;
/* Validate input parameters */ if (channelId >= EXP_VFB_MAX_CHANNELS) { Det_ReportError(EXP_VFB_MODULE_ID, 0, EXP_VFB_INVALID_CHANNEL_ID, EXP_VFB_E_PARAM); return; }
/* Call API function */ status = EXP_VFB_ReadChannel(channelId, &data);
/* Handle result */ switch (status) { case E_OK: /* Success - process data */ ProcessReceivedData(data); break;
case EXP_VFB_E_BUSY: /* Retry later */ ScheduleRetry(channelId); break;
case EXP_VFB_E_NOT_OK: /* Handle error */ HandleReadError(channelId); break;
default: /* Unknown error */ HandleUnknownError(status); break; } ```
